<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narseh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 302</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narseh was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> from 293 to 302, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-i">Shapur I</a>. He seized the throne from Bahram III and recorded his victory in the Paikuli inscription, which lists the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> kings who supported him. After early success against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> he was heavily defeated by the Caesar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galerius">Galerius</a> in 298 and had to accept the Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nisibis">Nisibis</a>, ceding lands in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and influence over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narseh.jpg" alt="Narseh" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narseh_relief.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
